# Web App Optimization (WordPress blocks · awesome-inspired)

The upstream awesome file named `web-app-optimization` is a **SvelteKit/Tailwind dump** — do not follow it. This rule is the project rewrite.
Defers to `.cursorrules` optimization_standards, `landing-page-image-quality`, `security-appsec`. Deeper queries/caching detail: `wp-performance` skill + `docs/standards/php-wordpress.md` §14.

## Performance (Web Vitals)
- **LCP:** prioritize hero/above-fold media; no blocking scripts before first paint; `fetchpriority="high"` on the hero image only
- **CLS:** explicit `width`/`height` or `aspect-ratio` on every image, video, and slider slide; reserve space for tabs/accordions that hydrate
- **INP:** keep click/tap handlers light; defer non-critical work; no layout thrash in scroll handlers
- Enqueue per block (`block.json` `style` / `viewScript`) so a page only loads what it renders — never enqueue a block's assets site-wide
- `loading="lazy"` below the fold; never on the LCP image
- Every `wp_enqueue_*` needs a version string tied to `TWORK_BUILDER_VERSION`

## Server side
- No `WP_Query` inside a render loop; no `posts_per_page => -1` on a query that grows
- Cache expensive render data in a transient with a deliberate TTL and a named invalidation point
- Prefer `wp_get_attachment_image()` so `srcset`/`sizes` are generated

## Markup & SEO
- Semantic HTML5 landmarks; one `h1` per page; heading levels in order inside a block
- Blocks that output headings should expose a heading-level control rather than hardcoding `h2`
- Do not invent SSR/hydration patterns — use the Interactivity API (`wp-interactivity-api` skill) when a block needs front-end state

## Accessibility
- Semantic controls over div-click; keyboard reachability for tabs, accordions, filters, and modals
- Visible focus; sufficient contrast; `aria-expanded` / `aria-controls` on disclosure UI
- ARIA only when native semantics are insufficient
- Informative images: specific `alt`; decorative: empty `alt`
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` in any scroll/entrance animation

## Responsive
- One adapting stylesheet, not a separate mobile build; breakpoints factored in while building desktop
- Do not remove or mutate existing responsive rules/utility classes when fixing a mobile view

## Reject
- SvelteKit · Tailwind-first · shadcn · Vite SPA scaffold “for performance”
- Rewriting a whole `style.scss` for a local LCP tweak
- Adding a new animation library (GSAP/Framer/AOS) when CSS or the in-tree approach works
